    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "ASK",
      "role_note": "terminal (Onda) — the command typed",
      "narration_text": "In the terminal: ask Claude to write a script that loads your held-out predictions CSV — two columns, predicted probability and true label — bins into ten confidence bins, plots the reliability diagram against the perfect-calibration diagonal, computes ECE and Brier score, fits temperature scaling on a validation split, and re-plots. Then takes the subset of rows where feature X is above its median as a shifted slice and recomputes ECE on that slice. Print both ECE values.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "command": "claude \"Write a Python script that:\n1. loads predictions.csv (predicted_prob, true_label)\n2. bins into 10 confidence bins\n3. plots reliability diagram vs diagonal\n4. computes ECE and Brier score\n5. fits temperature scaling on a val split, re-plots\n6. takes rows where feature_x > median as\n   'shifted slice', recomputes ECE\nPrint both ECE values: in-dist and shifted.\"",
            "topic": "COMPUTATIONAL SKEPTICISM — CALIBRATION",
            "segment": "RELIABILITY DIAGRAM — OWN MODEL",
            "greeting": "",
            "runningText": "generating reliability diagram script…",
            "output": [],
            "folderLabel": "@NikBearBrown",
            "modelLabel": "Fable 5",
            "effortLabel": "High"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B02.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 16,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-07-19T02:11:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "CODE",
      "role_note": "terminal (Onda) — read the output before running",
      "narration_text": "Read the three key operations before running. Calibration underscore curve from sklearn returns, per bin, the fraction of positives — the empirical positive rate — and the mean predicted probability. ECE is the mean absolute difference between those two. Temperature scaling fits a single scalar T on a validation split: T greater than one softens overconfident probabilities. And the shifted slice is the fairness-calibration intersection: does the model's overconfidence concentrate in the subgroup that matters most?",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeCodeBeat",
          "props": {
            "title": "reliability_diagram.py",
            "code": "# reliability_diagram.py — Claude Code output\nfrom sklearn.calibration import calibration_curve\nimport numpy as np\n\n# ECE: mean absolute gap between predicted and empirical\nppv, mean_pred = calibration_curve(\n    df[\"true_label\"], df[\"predicted_prob\"], n_bins=10\n)\nece = float(np.mean(np.abs(ppv - mean_pred)))\n\n# temperature scaling: T > 1 softens overconfidence\n# optimized on held-out validation split\nT = optimize_temperature(val_probs, val_labels)\nscaled = sigmoid(logit(probs) / T)\n\n# shifted slice: high-value subgroup\nshifted = df[df[\"feature_x\"] > df[\"feature_x\"].median()]\nece_shifted = compute_ece(shifted)",
            "sparkLine": "RELIABILITY DIAGRAM — OWN MODEL"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B03.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 16,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-07-19T02:11:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "OUTPUT — run",
      "role_note": "Manim animation: B04_ReliabilityDiagram — two panels side by side",
      "narration_text": "Run it. Left panel: in-distribution reliability diagram. The curve tracks the diagonal reasonably well — ECE is point-zero-eight. Right panel: shifted slice, the high feature-X subgroup. The curve bends away from the diagonal at high confidence. ECE jumps to point-nineteen. The model that looks calibrated on its training distribution is systematically overconfident in the deployment regime it matters most for. That gap does not appear until you plot the shifted slice.",
      "visual_intent": "Manim B04_ReliabilityDiagram: two reliability diagrams side by side — left (in-distribution, ECE=0.08, curve near diagonal) and right (shifted slice, ECE=0.19, overconfidence zone highlighted); ECE values animate in; a 'gap' arrow in the right panel",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "motion": "fade",
        "manim": {
          "scene_class": "B04_ReliabilityDiagram",
          "file": "vox_scenes.py"
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 19,
      "build": {
