        "src": "manim/B04.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim:B04_ReliabilityDiagram",
        "at": "2026-07-19T02:11:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "CHANGE — check and revise",
      "role_note": "terminal (Onda) — lock the prediction first, then apply temperature scaling",
      "narration_text": "Before re-running with temperature scaling, lock a prediction. Ask Claude to add a step at the top of the script: prompt the user for their guessed ECE on the shifted slice, hash it, write it to predlock.log. Then run temperature scaling. After, resolve: print the guessed ECE, the actual ECE, and whether the hash still verifies. Calibration on training distribution does not survive a distribution shift — and the locked prediction is the only way to know whether you knew that.",
      "shot": {
